    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Isaac Paredes** (68.00) headline our offense as the clear priority starts. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Sasaki, while **Isaac Paredes** leverages a significant platoon advantage and an optimal slot in the three-hole to anchor our production. **Josh Naylor** also cracks the 60+ threshold, offering reliable stability in the UTIL spot despite a middle-of-the-road matchup against May. While we are aggressive on speed, we have exercised discipline with our floor; players like **Zach McKinstry** and **Travis Bazzana** were benched firmly below our 40.0 efficiency floor, as both face elite arm talent that stifles their projected output.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 54.83 score. While **Austin Riley** offers intriguing power upside, the combination of his lower spot in the order and the efficiency metrics of our OF and UTIL starters squeezed him out. We are keeping a close eye on **Corbin Carroll** (57.20); while his raw talent is elite, he is contending with a tough assignment against Tolle and a slight degradation in his score due to an elite hold SP matchup that suppresses his primary weapon\u2014stolen bases. **Henry Bolte** remains a high-variance play at 59.58, but his favorable matchup against the hittable Lugo makes him an essential start to chase the category upside we need to maintain our pace in this 5x5 format.",
